    "explanationEn": "Part (c) is the discriminator and tests oxygen debt (excess post-exercise oxygen consumption). During vigorous exercise some muscle respires anaerobically and lactic acid accumulates; extra oxygen is still needed after exercise to oxidise it, so the breathing rate does not fall back at once. \"To repay the oxygen missed during exercise\" is the right direction, but lactic acid must be named for the answer to be complete.\nPart (d) confuses the respiratory system with thermoregulation. Humans lose heat mainly by sweating and vasodilation of skin blood vessels; heat loss through breathing is a small fraction in humans (it is prominent in dogs and similar animals). The part asks candidates to separate \"happens at the same time\" from \"is the cause\" — the body is indeed still hot, but that is not why breathing stays fast.",
