    "explanationEn": "The correct explanation in (b) is that energy transfer between levels is very inefficient (roughly ten per cent), most of the rest being lost as heat from respiration or locked in parts not eaten or not digested. By the fourth or fifth level there is too little energy left to support a population. Writing only \"energy is lost\" without the approximate proportion or the routes of loss is incomplete.\nPart (d) is about the full consequences of eutrophication. The reasoning takes only the first step of the food chain and overlooks that the algae bloom, then die, and that bacterial decomposition consumes large amounts of dissolved oxygen, so the deoxygenated water kills the fish instead. The structural error is cutting a multi-step causal chain off at the step that suits the conclusion.",
    "markingScheme": "(a) 2 分 —— 食物鏈次序正確（1）；四個營養級名稱正確（1）。\n(b) 2 分 —— 指出傳遞效率低（約百分之十）（1）；說明能量以呼吸熱能／未被攝食或未消化部分流失（1）。\n(c) 3 分 —— 藻華（1）；藻類死亡後細菌分解消耗溶氧（1）；水中缺氧導致魚類死亡（1）。次序須成鏈，散列現象最多得 2 分。\n(d) 1 分 —— 指出推論截斷於第一步，忽略藻類死亡、細菌分解耗氧、最終缺氧致魚類死亡。\n本題所列分數為本平台練習用尺度，並非香港考試及評核局的分數分配。參考答案只列必達步驟與判準，刻意不提供可直接抄錄的完整答卷。交卷後請逐項對照自評，機器不會為本題評分。",
