    "content": "一名健康人士在炎熱天氣下進行戶外工作三小時，期間只飲用少量水。\n(a) 描述其血液滲透濃度的變化，並說明身體如何偵測此變化。\n(b) 描述抗利尿激素（ADH）分泌量的變化及其對腎臟的作用。\n(c) 說明尿液的體積與濃度將如何改變。\n(d) 若該人士其後一次過大量飲水，描述身體的調節反應，並解釋為何負反饋機制不會令體內水分持續增加。",
    "explanation": "本題考的是一條完整的負反饋鏈，失分多數源於鏈條斷裂而非個別知識點錯誤。常見的斷點有三：一是只寫「ADH 增加」而未說出其作用位置（腎小管及集尿管的水分重吸收）；二是把 ADH 的作用寫成「令尿液減少」而未經重吸收這一步，等於跳過機制；三是 (d) 只描述反向變化而未回答「為何不會持續增加」。\n(d) 的正確答案須點明負反饋的定義：反應本身會消除引發它的刺激。血液被稀釋後 ADH 下降、排出多餘水分，滲透濃度回升至正常，刺激消失，反應隨之停止 —— 系統因此圍繞設定點振盪，而非單向偏離。只答「因為身體會調節」並未觸及機制。",
    "referenceAnswer": "(a) 因大量出汗而水分流失，飲水不足，血液的滲透濃度上升（血液變得較濃）。\n下視丘的滲透壓感受器偵測到此上升。\n\n(b) 下視丘受刺激後，腦垂體後葉分泌的抗利尿激素（ADH）增加。\nADH 經血液運送至腎臟，令腎小管遠端及集尿管的管壁對水的通透性上升，水分由濾液被重吸收回血液的量因而增加。\n\n(c) 尿液體積減少，濃度上升（顏色較深）。此為水分被大量重吸收的直接結果。\n\n(d) 大量飲水後，血液的滲透濃度下降（血液被稀釋）。下視丘的滲透壓感受器偵測到此下降，腦垂體後葉分泌的 ADH 減少。腎小管遠端及集尿管對水的通透性下降，水分重吸收減少，故排出大量稀釋的尿液，血液的滲透濃度回升至正常水平。\n\n負反饋不會令體內水分持續增加，因為【反應本身會消除引發它的刺激】。血液被稀釋引發 ADH 下降；ADH 下降令多餘水分被排出；水分排出後血液的滲透濃度回升，稀釋這個刺激隨之消失，ADH 分泌回復正常水平，排水反應亦停止。系統因此在設定點附近來回調節，而非朝單一方向持續偏離。",
    "marks": 9,
    "referenceAnswerEn": "(a) Heavy sweating with insufficient drinking causes water loss, so the osmotic concentration of the blood rises (the blood becomes more concentrated).\nOsmoreceptors in the hypothalamus detect this rise.\n\n(b) The stimulated hypothalamus causes the posterior pituitary to secrete more antidiuretic hormone (ADH).\nADH is carried in the blood to the kidneys, where it raises the permeability to water of the walls of the distal tubules and collecting ducts, so more water is reabsorbed from the filtrate back into the blood.\n\n(c) The volume of urine falls and its concentration rises (it is darker). This follows directly from the greater water reabsorption.\n\n(d) After drinking a large volume, the osmotic concentration of the blood falls (the blood is diluted). The hypothalamic osmoreceptors detect the fall and the posterior pituitary secretes less ADH. The distal tubules and collecting ducts become less permeable to water, less water is reabsorbed, and a large volume of dilute urine is excreted, so the osmotic concentration returns towards normal.\n\nNegative feedback prevents the body water from rising indefinitely because THE RESPONSE REMOVES THE STIMULUS THAT CAUSED IT. Dilution of the blood causes ADH to fall; falling ADH causes the excess water to be excreted; once it is excreted the osmotic concentration rises again, the dilution stimulus disappears, ADH returns to its normal level and the response stops. The system therefore corrects back and forth about a set point instead of drifting steadily in one direction.",
    "contentEn": "A healthy person works outdoors for three hours in hot weather, drinking only a little water.\n(a) Describe the change in the osmotic concentration of the blood and how the body detects it.\n(b) Describe the change in secretion of antidiuretic hormone (ADH) and its effect on the kidneys.\n(c) State how the volume and concentration of the urine change.\n(d) If the person then drinks a large volume of water at once, describe the regulatory response, and explain why negative feedback prevents the body water from rising indefinitely.",
    "explanationEn": "This question tests a complete negative-feedback chain, and most marks are lost through a break in the chain rather than a wrong fact. Three breaks are common: writing \"ADH increases\" without saying where it acts (water reabsorption in the tubules and collecting ducts); writing that ADH \"reduces urine\" without going through reabsorption, which skips the mechanism; and, in (d), describing the reverse changes without answering why the water does not keep rising.\nThe correct answer to (d) must state what negative feedback means: the response removes the stimulus that produced it. Once the blood is diluted, ADH falls, the excess water is excreted, the osmotic concentration returns towards normal, the stimulus disappears and the response stops — so the system oscillates about a set point rather than drifting one way. \"Because the body regulates itself\" does not reach the mechanism.",
    "markingScheme": "(a) 2 分 —— 血液滲透濃度上升（1）；下視丘滲透壓感受器偵測（1）。\n(b) 3 分 —— ADH 分泌增加（1）；點名腦垂體後葉（1）；作用於腎小管遠端及集尿管，提高對水的通透性令重吸收增加（1）。只寫「令尿量減少」而無重吸收得 0 分。\n(c) 2 分 —— 體積減少（1）；濃度上升（1）。\n(d) 2 分 —— 描述反向調節（ADH 下降、重吸收減少、排出大量稀尿）（1）；說明負反饋的機制係反應消除刺激，故系統在設定點附近振盪（1）。只答「身體會自我調節」不得該分。\n本題所列分數為本平台練習用尺度，並非香港考試及評核局的分數分配。參考答案只列必達步驟與判準，刻意不提供可直接抄錄的完整答卷。交卷後請逐項對照自評，機器不會為本題評分。",
    "markingSchemeEn": "(a) 2 marks — osmotic concentration of the blood rises (1); detected by hypothalamic osmoreceptors (1).\n(b) 3 marks — ADH secretion increases (1); posterior pituitary named (1); acting on the distal tubules and collecting ducts to raise water permeability and hence reabsorption (1). \"Makes less urine\" without reabsorption earns nothing.\n(c) 2 marks — volume falls (1); concentration rises (1).\n(d) 2 marks — the reverse response described (ADH falls, less reabsorption, large volume of dilute urine) (1); negative feedback explained as the response removing the stimulus, so the system oscillates about a set point (1). \"The body regulates itself\" does not earn this mark.\nThe marks shown are a practice scale used on this platform, not an HKEAA mark allocation. The reference answer lists the required steps and criteria rather than a copyable model script. Compare your own work against it point by point; nothing here is machine-marked.",
